    "narrative": "Today\u2019s roster for LawDog hinges on capitalizing on soft-tossing lefties and favorable lineup slots to drive efficiency. **Lawrence Butler** (68.54) leads the charge as our strongest play; he benefits from a massive 13% boost in his dynamic platoon against the right-handed Tyler Mahle, compounded by wind blowing out at the venue. Similarly, **Daulton Varsho** (67.01) is a mandatory start against Burrows, utilizing his high-efficiency profile to anchor our outfield output. Both **Geraldo Perdomo** (63.13) and **Tyler Freeman** (61.08) are highlighted as key contributors today, specifically due to their high-leverage spots in the batting order and favorable park environments that mitigate the risks posed by their respective left-handed matchups.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the benching of **Jonathan Aranda** (44.44). While his xwOBA of 0.376 is respectable, he ultimately fell short of the starting threshold due to a significant 12% penalty in his platoon split against Cameron, which effectively neutralized his base projection. Meanwhile, we are closely monitoring the lineup status of **Gavin Sheets**, **Luis Arraez**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Matt Chapman**; because these spots are currently \"Lineup Pending,\" any drastic shifts in their projected batting order could jeopardize their projected efficiency. We continue to manage our caps carefully while keeping an eye on **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Ryan Waldschmidt**, both of whom remain unavailable due to their current IL and MiLB designations, respectively.",
